The '''XVIII Simlympiad Opening Ceremony''' was held in '''[[Okami|Okashi]] (now renamed as '''Okami'''), Okaiken''' in 2013. The ceremony served as the formal inauguration of the XVIII Simlympiad, themed around the concept of "Harmony through Unity." The event was produced and aired by the Official Broadcaster of the XVIII Simlympiad (OBS) and featured a narrative focused on the four elements—Fire, Earth, Air, and Water—that define the cultural heritage of the Sanese people.

==Ceremony Highlights==
The ceremony was structured into several thematic segments:
* '''The Four Elements:''' A theatrical display showing how Fire, Earth, Air, and Water created the islands of Okashi.
* '''Air Segment:''' A torch-lit performance where the Air symbol of the Okashi flag was formed, followed by the creation of the Simlympic Rings.
* '''Struggle on the Sea:''' A dramatic presentation of the "Sea Dragon," representing the historical relationship between the Sanese people and the ocean.
* '''Cultural Performances:''' Included a presentation of the planet [[Adonia]] and a musical performance by the idol group [[w:AKB48|AKB48]].
* '''Lighting of the Flame:''' The Simlympic flame was carried into the stadium by athlete '''Asami Hiroyuna''' and passed to '''Honda Iemitsu'''. The cauldron was ignited via a unique pulley system that moved the flame from the stadium floor to its final position.

==Official Personnel==
* '''Commentator:''' Tobei Kobayashi
* '''International Simlympic Committee President:''' Joe Simon
* '''Dignitaries:''' Various representatives from the 44 participating nations.

